//
// A SEQUENCE ALTERNATION AFTER FIXED ELEMENTS IS REFUSED (`@FR-P-Alt`, `@FR-P-Opt`).  An OPTIONAL
// group may follow fixed elements (loft#2048); a multi-element alternation `( A B | C )` is the
// whole slice pattern, and after a fixed element it is refused by name rather than read as
// something else.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal is new with loft#2048's lowering.
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the construct.
// HOLDS: the optional group after a fixed element, in the sibling file, on both trees.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: a multi-element alternation `( … | … )` is the whole slice pattern

enum Tok { Num { n: integer }, Kw { k: integer }, Op { o: integer } }

fn main() {
  v: vector<Tok> = [Num { n: 1 }, Kw { k: 2 }, Op { o: 3 }];
  r = match v { [Num { n }, (Kw { k } Op { o } | Op { o })] => n, _ => -1 };
  println("{r}");
}
